+# 138 · A window start computed as the window's index times its length proved equal to the remainder form
+
+[← All examples](../README.md)
+
+| Verdict | Categories | Severity if shipped | Change | Verified unit | Approach |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **⚠ Unverifiable** | functional, no-false-positive | none | refactor, behaviour change not intended | [`Window#counted`](../../examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java) | [B9: Regression verification](../../lib/README.md) |
+
+> Crosscut's `Window` counter computes the start of the window a reading falls in as `nowNanos - nowNanos % windowNanos`. A rewrite names the window's index first, `nowNanos / windowNanos`, and multiplies it back: the form a reader expects, and the one that gives the index a name for a log line or a key. The two are equal by Java's division identity, `d == (d / p) * p + d % p` for every `d` and `p`, which no engine proved within a minute until the tool's own checker learned it: a quotient times its divisor is now the dividend less the remainder, the same bits the old version computes, and the proof over every counter, reading and window takes 0.1 s.
+
+Tags: [resilience](../README.md#tag-resilience), [clocks-and-time](../README.md#tag-clocks-and-time), [rounding](../README.md#tag-rounding), [record-components](../README.md#tag-record-components), [own-checker](../README.md#tag-own-checker)
+
+## The change
+
+Compute the window's index, `long index = nowNanos / windowNanos`, and its start as `index * windowNanos`, in place of `nowNanos - nowNanos % windowNanos`. The tests are unchanged.
+
+**Before** ([`Window.java`](../../examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java), line 26):
+
+```java
+        if (windowNanos <= 0 || nowNanos < startNanos) {
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("the window must be positive and time must not go back");
+        }
+        long start = nowNanos - nowNanos % windowNanos;
+        return start == startNanos ? new Window(startNanos, count + 1) : new Window(start, 1);
+    }
+}
+```
+
+**After:**
+
+```java
+        if (windowNanos <= 0 || nowNanos < startNanos) {
+            throw new IllegalArgumentException("the window must be positive and time must not go back");
+        }
+        // The window the reading falls in, counted from zero, and where it starts.
+        long index = nowNanos / windowNanos;
+        long start = index * windowNanos;
+        return start == startNanos ? new Window(startNanos, count + 1) : new Window(start, 1);
+    }
+}
+```
+
+<details><summary>Patch</summary>
+
+```diff
+diff --git a/examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java b/examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java
+index 8214e20..4ef4c34 100644
+--- a/examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java
++++ b/examples/apps/crosscut/src/main/java/net/terminalvalue/crosscut/ratelimit/Window.java
+@@ -26,7 +26,9 @@ public record Window(long startNanos, long count) {
+         if (windowNanos <= 0 || nowNanos < startNanos) {
+             throw new IllegalArgumentException("the window must be positive and time must not go back");
+         }
+-        long start = nowNanos - nowNanos % windowNanos;
++        // The window the reading falls in, counted from zero, and where it starts.
++        long index = nowNanos / windowNanos;
++        long start = index * windowNanos;
+         return start == startNanos ? new Window(startNanos, count + 1) : new Window(start, 1);
+     }
+ }
+```
+
+</details>
